WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.879
This is a production of Cornell
University

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:16.640
Hi graduates! Hello from Ithaca!
Congratulations! Can you believe it?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:24.160
Class of 2020 Ag Sciences!
We are proud of you!

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.840
Hey guys, not only are we proud of you. I hope you're proud of yourselves and the

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.920
accomplishments you have made over the last four years

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.000
or two years.
We are so proud of what you've

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.600
accomplished in your time at Cornell.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.920
It's hard to believe this, but you are about to enter a new phase.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.440
You are turning from student to Cornell alum. Welcome to a lifetime relationship

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.680
with people from around the world, and
when it comes to ag

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.520
sciences -- unless you didn't know this
already --

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.280
let me reiterate you now have your
forever home.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.240
Guys, the world needs you. I know 
I've had a number of you in my classes.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.600
I've gotten to know pretty well all of

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.560
you. Like basically.
I know you, all of you, and i just want to

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.560
say that your Cornell training, 
I am totally positive has really

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.119
prepared you to take on whatever
challenges come

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:33.439
towards you. You know research that
you've been doing,

00:01:33.439 --> 00:01:37.200
working with other professors, 
critical thinking skills,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.240
time management all the things that you
first took with

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.799
us in our introductory course and have
taken on your additional courses. So

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:50.000
please, please, do something to help this planet out. I  have total confidence in all of you.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
 

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.060
We have seen you in your best and in your worst. We have walked with you and talked with

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.600
you and supported you.
And we want you to know that we have

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:08.720
tremendous faith in you.
You are incredibly resilient.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.120
This is a moment when your resilience
has been tested,

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.520
and what you have learned is that you
can do anything.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.599
Be kind to yourself remember to be
flexible

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:25.280
and know that we're here for you.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.800
I'll end by saying I think all of you
know that

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.680
I was born in Italy and family in the
Italian culture is extremely important.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:39.040
And i just want to say that you've all
now become part of 'mia famiglia' and so I

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.080
want to say 'benvenuti a la famiglia' which basically

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.920
means welcome to the family: the
agricultural sciences family

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.000
the Cornell family. You will always be
Cornellians

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.599
and always be AgSci majors. So we would
love to

00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:57.120
stay in touch with all of you. Please let
Kari and I know what

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.280
you're up to down the road, when you have families, no matter where you are in the

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.760
world, we'd love to hear from you.
So I'll end by saying congratulations

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.560
once again to all of you and to your
families

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.879
that have supported you and we look
forward to seeing you.

00:03:11.879 --> 00:03:23.540
Congratulations 2020!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.519
This has been a production of Cornell
University,

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:42.080
on the web at cornell dot edu

